    "updated_at": "2022-09-20T14:37:27Z",
    "body": "I was complaining about this to a friend last night, and he pointed out that you can click on the entries in the Emojipedia to expand them. In the expanded form, they show known history of the emoji rendering.\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4605384/191286789-489e5126-37fe-4270-aecd-d218549a4380.png)\r\n\r\nFor the Microsoft case, it looks like this was screwed up in an early update of Windows 11 that [launched the fluent emoji set](https://emojipedia.org/microsoft/windows-11-november-2021-update/).\r\n\r\nThis doesn't solve the issue at hand, but it does explain why it seems to be restricted to Windows 11 (and also informs me that we should slowly expect this issue to get worse over the coming years as more people switch to 11, unless Microsoft fixes their emojis).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
